Planetary Grid Reference

Extracted from the public AEGIS implementation at commit
212d2a4355bd555469722b1c8f082b128b9fd231 (feat-mgrs).
AEGIS: Application for Exploration Geospatial Integration and Scheduling.
Extraction and packaging changes: 2026.

Selected lunar coordinate formatting aspects are ported/adapted from Python LGRS
v0.4.0, commit 1f11a12ac20e4f4aab89805535319252a2abd2eb:
https://github.com/rbeyer/lgrs
Copyright (c) 2026, Ethan I. Schaefer (eschaefer@seti.org).
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE.
LGRS was developed at the SETI Institute based on open USGS code.
Contributors credited upstream include Ross Beyer and Mark McClernan.
The TypeScript port uses explicit numerical boundary handling, a functional
buffer-oriented API, and additional Earth analog and grid-planning algorithms.

Lunar projection parameters, coordinate conventions and lettering tables follow
McClernan et al. (2025), USGS Techniques and Methods 11-E1:
https://doi.org/10.3133/tm11E1
Earth analog ACC lettering draws on the USGS terrestrial training-grid release:
https://doi.org/10.5066/P14KSANW
The worldwide Earth ACC area prefix is an AEGIS-originated convention.
Earth MGRS lettering follows NGA Universal Grids and Grid Reference Systems.
These source references do not imply endorsement of this package.

The map projection fast paths in src/mapProjection.ts adapt proj4js formulas;
proj4 is also an external runtime dependency. Its notice follows in full.

